We appreciate all of your feedback on Corsairs Legacy. Our team analyzed it, and from the release day began to work on changes that players wanted to see. The first Early Access update for Corsairs Legacy was released today, and we will continue to expand the game regularly.

Below you can find the list of changes included in the update:
[olist]
you can capture and transfer to any ship in the game;

the gameplay logic of the quests changed; markers have been removed in some places so that players can solve the quests on their own;

the required amount of land movement reduced;

all chests in Barbados now have loot;

during ground battles, a marker has been added to enemies above their heads, informing about an attack on the main character (similar to Assassin's Creed: Unity) to increase the ability to parry a blow;

the operation of the camera on the stairs in the prison fixed;

fixed a critical bug of the absence of Spanish soldiers on the Tobago beach;

fixed bug with invisible English soldiers in prison and lighthouse.
[/olist]
Note! The new version removes the progress. Progress saving will be added in the next update.

List of tasks that should be included in the next few updates:
[olist]
traders will appear in the game;

the possibility of character development will be added;

the city of Bridgetown will be added;

additional side activities will appear;

an opportunity to usefully spend all earned funds will be added.
[/olist]
We've decided to focus all efforts on expanding Corsairs Legacy and put plans for future releases on hold until the current game is refined with player feedback.

For us to be able to improve and expand Corsairs Legacy, it is important to have stable sales, and for this, we need to have a positive rating on Steam. If you agree with our direction of development, please leave a positive review on Steam so that the game can reach a higher user rating. We will be very grateful to you.
